{"reference":"Luke 15","book":"Luke","chapter":15,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"The Two Sons","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The final story is not only about the younger son's return. It also portrays the father's costly welcome and the elder son's resentment. Because the father continues to appeal to the elder son, whose response is left unstated, the story ends as an unresolved invitation rather than a simple formula for conversion.","verse_refs":["Luke 15:11-32"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_luke_015_ac0f72d6454476cf285b62b8"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}